  "note": "Stage D0 (issue #335, 2026-08-12) appended 85 probes and raised WIRE_DIVERGE_BASELINE from 10 to 63, and Stages D1 and D2 lowered it to 52. NOTHING REGRESSED. The first enumeration covered the precedence table and the field-expression operand positions - 24 of the reference grammar's 33 productions. Stage D0 enumerated all 33; the nine that had never been probed carry two classes on their own. The rise is the enumeration widening from a subset of the grammar to the whole of it, not decay. See accept_surface/grammar_slots.json, accept_surface/PROVENANCE.md section 'Stage D0' and the doc block above TOTAL/AGREE/DIVERGE in pulsus-traceql/tests/accept_surface.rs. Issue #460 closed D17 (compare()'s two extra arities), moving its two probes reject->accept on both axes: WIRE_AGREE_BASELINE 254 -> 256 and WIRE_DIVERGE_BASELINE 52 -> 50. The baseline is directional and this move is toward FEWER divergences.",
